package townframe:dayframe@0.4.0;

/// What a wasm micro component is built against: the host-facing `micro-client` world plus the
/// one network interface a micro may use. `wasi:http/client` reaches only `http://dispatch.local`
/// (`GET`/`POST /xrpc/<nsid>`); every runtime's egress refuses anything else and hands what it
/// admits to the host's `MicroDispatch`, acting as the micro's own identity.
///
/// Hosts keep linking `micro-client`: `wasi:*` imports reach a runtime through its WASI
/// implementation, not through the host bindings, and a component whose code never calls the
/// client does not import it.
world micro-guest {
  include micro-client;
  import wasi:http/client@0.3.0;
}
